guration**\\\\n2. In the left-hand menu, navigate to `Appearance` -> `Themes`.\\\\n3. Click the `Add New` button at the top of the page.\\\\n4. In the search bar, type `Astra` and press Enter.\\\\n5. Locate the \\\\\\\"Astra\\\\\\\" theme in the search results and click the `Install` button.\\\\n6. After installation is complete, click the `Activate` button.\\\\n\\\\n**Part 3: Required Plugin Installation**\\\\n7. In the left-hand menu, navigate to `Plugins` -> `Add New`.\\\\n8. Search for, install, and activate the plugin: `Ultimate Member – User Profile, Registration, Login, Member Directory, Content Restriction & Membership Plugin`.\\\\n9. Return to `Plugins` -> `Add New`. Search for, install, and activate the plugin: `Contact Form by WPForms – Drag & Drop Form Builder for WordPress`.\\\\n10. Return to `Plugins` -> `Add New`. Search for, install, and activate the plugin: `Elementor Website Builder`.\\\\n\\\\n**Part 4: Website Structure (Page Creation)**\\\\n11. Create the public-facing pages. For each page name listed below, navigate to `Pages` -> `Add New`, enter the name as the title, and click `Publish`.\\\\n    * Home\\\\n    * About Us\\\\n    * News & Updates\\\\n    * Contact Us\\\\n    * Resident Portal\\\\n12. Create the private, resident-only pages. For each page name listed below, navigate to `Pages` -> `Add New`, enter the name as the title, and click `Publish`.\\\\n    * Community Documents\\\\n    * Meeting Minutes\\\\n    * Financial Reports\\\\n\\\\n**Part 5: Basic Configuration**\\\\n13. Set the \\\\\\\"Home\\\\\\\" page as the website's front page. Navigate to `Settings` -> `Reading`. Under \\\\\\\"Your homepage displays\\\\\\\", select \\\\\\\"A static page\\\\\\\". From the \\\\\\\"Homepage\\\\\\\" dropdown, select \\\\\\\"Home\\\\\\\". Click `Save Changes`.\\\\n14. Create a primary navigation menu. Navigate to `Appearance` -> `Menus`. Enter `Main Menu` as the menu name and click `Create Menu`.\\\\n15. From the \\\\\\\"Pages\\\\\\\" box on the left, check the boxes for `Home`, `About Us`, `News & Updates`, `Contact Us`, and `Resident Portal`. Click `Add to Menu`.\\\\n16. Under \\\\\\\"Menu Settings\\\\\\\" at the bottom, check the box for \\\\\\\"Primary Menu\\\\\\\". Click `Save Menu`.\\\\n\\\\n**Part 6: User Roles and Content Restriction**\\\\n17. Create a \\\\\\\"Resident\\\\\\\" user role. Navigate to `Ultimate Member` -> `User Roles`. Click `Add New`. Set the \\\\\\\"Role Title\\\\\\\" to `Resident` and click `Create Role`.\\\\n18. Restrict access to private pages. For each private page (`Community Documents`, `Meeting Minutes`, `Financial Reports`), navigate to its edit screen. Find the \\\\\\\"Ultimate Member\\\\\\\" content restriction box.\\\\n19. In the \\\\\\\"Ultimate Member\\\\\\\" box, enable restriction for \\\\\\\"Logged in users\\\\\\\" and select only the \\\\\\\"Resident\\\\\\\" role. Update the page to save the changes.\\\\n\\\\n**Part 7: Create a Simple Contact Form**\\\\n20. Create the contact form. Navigate to `WPForms` -> `Add New`. Name your form `General Contact Form` and select the `Simple Contact Form` template.\\\\n21. Review the default fields (Name, Email, Message) and click `Save`.\\\\n22. Add the contact form to the \\\\\\\"Contact Us\\\\\\\" page. Edit the page, add the \\\\\\\"WPForms\\\\\\\" block, and select the `General Contact Form` you just created. Update the page to save.\\\"\\n}\\n###20250719-PHASE-EXECUTION-02###\"}]},{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"###CALL_RESULTS-2025-07-19T20:15:50.803Z###\\nSYSTEM MESSAGE\\nFrom: Operations Department, System Call Directorate\\nTo: 1\\nType: Call Results\\n##\\n{\\n  \\\"result\\\": \\\"{\\\\n  \\\\\\\"results\\\\\\\": [\\\\n    {\\\\n      \\\\\\\"callID\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"20250719-PHASE-EXECUTION-02\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"status\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"SUCCESS\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"details\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Phase shift to EXECUTION approved by user.\\\\\\\"\\\\n    }\\\\n  ]\\\\n}\\\"\\n}\\n###CALL_RESULTS-2025