ch results and click the `Install` button.\\\\n6. After installation is complete, click the `Activate` button.\\\\n\\\\n**Part 3: Required Plugin Installation**\\\\n7. In the left-hand menu, navigate to `Plugins` -> `Add New`.\\\\n8. Search for, install, and activate the plugin: `Ultimate Member – User Profile, Registration, Login, Member Directory, Content Restriction & Membership Plugin`.\\\\n9. Return to `Plugins` -> `Add New`. Search for, install, and activate the plugin: `Contact Form by WPForms – Drag & Drop Form Builder for WordPress`.\\\\n10. Return to `Plugins` -> `Add New`. Search for, install, and activate the plugin: `Elementor Website Builder`.\\\\n\\\\n**Part 4: Website Structure (Page Creation)**\\\\n11. Create the public-facing pages. For each page name listed below, navigate to `Pages` -> `Add New`, enter the name as the title, and click `Publish`.\\\\n    * Home\\\\n    * About Us\\\\n    * News & Updates\\\\n    * Contact Us\\\\n    * Resident Portal\\\\n12. Create the private, resident-only pages. For each page name listed below, navigate to `Pages` -> `Add New`, enter the name as the title, and click `Publish`.\\\\n    * Community Documents\\\\n    * Meeting Minutes\\\\n    * Financial Reports\\\\n\\\\n**Part 5: Basic Configuration**\\\\n13. Set the \\\\\\\"Home\\\\\\\" page as the website's front page. Navigate to `Settings` -> `Reading`. Under \\\\\\\"Your homepage displays\\\\\\\", select \\\\\\\"A static page\\\\\\\". From the \\\\\\\"Homepage\\\\\\\" dropdown, select \\\\\\\"Home\\\\\\\". Click `Save Changes`.\\\\n14. Create a primary navigation menu. Navigate to `Appearance` -> `Menus`. Enter `Main Menu` as the menu name and click `Create Menu`.\\\\n15. From the \\\\\\\"Pages\\\\\\\" box on the left, check the boxes for `Home`, `About Us`, `News & Updates`, `Contact Us`, and `Resident Portal`. Click `Add to Menu`.\\\\n16. Under \\\\\\\"Menu Settings\\\\\\\" at the bottom, check the box for \\\\\\\"Primary Menu\\\\\\\". Click `Save Menu`.\\